If memory serves:

One-two!  One-two!  And through!  And through!
The vorpal sword went snicker-snack!

It has been a common misconception that Snickersnee derives from this.
In fact, it is the sword of the lord high executioner in the Mikado,
a Gilbert & Sullivan play.  One good netter (Andrew?) was kind enuf to
post the relevant verse earlier in this thread.

Samurai aspiring to the post of executioner may be disappointed to
hear that they can no longer name their katanas "Snickersnee" on turn
1 for a rich damage bonus.  Such a katana may still appear in the
manners that artifacts generally do, tho.


